# @dump: own counts wat
# @build: v8 release
# The literal piece is 27 bytes, a constant length in the dynamic helper's
# last class `[16, 32)`: it copies as that class's first and last 16 bytes,
# four `i64` loads before four stores, with no `memory.copy` (#1696). The
# name's length is known only at run time and calls `rt:memory_copy`.
fn owner(name: string) -> string:
    "the account owner is named " + name
